WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.310
<i>While we were searching for the Number in one of the seven Ruins,</i>

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.620
<i>the Duel Spirit Mach appeared before us and a Duel began.</i>

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.570
<i>However, the guy told us that Shark's and Nach's souls are at stake in this Duel!</i>

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:16.990
<i>Shark! Nasch! I'll definitely save you!</i>

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:21.770
Ryouga!

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.200
Go, Gagaga Magician! Attack the Defense Position Monster!

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.820
A door!

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.340
A Hero of the past once said this:

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:48.510
"The bond we share with others shall open new paths."

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.310
Ryouga!

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.600
I'll activate Druid Wyd's effect!

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.770
When this Monster is destroyed,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.500
I can activate a Continuous Magic, Labyrinth of Decisions, from my hand!

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.080
Then, I send two cards from my hand to the Graveyard,

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.710
to activate the Continuous Trap, Unfair Treaty!

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.740
These two cards are...

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.300
What?!

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.740
From above this time?!

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.680
<i>If I could bring back my original power, I would be able to escape from here...</i>

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.140
Hold on, Shark!

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:27.620
Go, Gagaga Kid!

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.570
Direct Attack that guy!

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.510
At this moment, those two cards shall corner you both!

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.200
Labyrinth of Decisions' effect activates!

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:48.480
When the battle is over after the opponent's attack,

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.770
I can pay 600 of my Life,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.820
to send one card from the opposing player's hand to the Graveyard.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.600
From <i>my</i> hand?

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:59.370
Then I activate the Continuous Trap, Unfair Treaty!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.620
With this card, when I activate the effect of my Continuous Magic

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.880
where I would have to pay Life Points as a cost,

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.570
you pay those Life Points instead!

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:10.560
I do...?!

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.650
I see! His aim is...

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.730
Now hurry up and discard from your hand!

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.800
Damn!

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.620
I send one card to the Graveyard!

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:27.970
This is a combo to destroy our hand and our Life.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.400
So this is our trial...?!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:33.850
<i>Our trial...</i>

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:38.710
<i>"The bond we share with others shall open new paths."</i>

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.310
That's it!

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.170
It means a door will open for Shark and Nasch when we attack!

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.050
Wh-What?!

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:50.910
With his combo, our Life will be chipped away if we attack.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:55.250
But if we don't attack, we have no chance of saving Shark and Nasch.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.140
Now!

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.050
What will you do to survive this trial?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:29.560
<i>Being best friends doesn't mean we always were</i>

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.630
<i>That's pretty much true</i>

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:40.090
<i>I found you during our serious battles</i>

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.640
<i>The other me inside myself</i>

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.520
<i>Awakening from within the conflict</i>

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:54.860
<i>A turn for a chance! Seize it! Draw!</i>

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.070
<i>Duel! Dualism!</i>

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.950
<i>These cards are polished to fit each other</i>

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.580
<i>My fated opponent is my heart reflected through the mirror</i>

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:08.660
<i>And if we end up with a "tie" in the end,</i>

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:17.130
<i>when we fall, all covered with mud, we'll praise each other</i>

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.960
What will you do to survive this trial?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.040
Trial, my rear! You're screwing with us!

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:40.590
"A Recollection from the Past:
 Durbe and the White Horse - a Legendary Phantom"

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.170
I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Magician and Gagaga Kid!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:45.470
With these two Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.800
Xyz Summon!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.720
Appear, Number 39!

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.520
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.650
With this, I end my turn!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.570
So this is your Number?

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.440
My turn!

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:04.610
Draw!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:08.280
I Summon Manipulative Druid Drewes!

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.410
When this card is successfully Summoned,

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.460
I can Special Summon one Druid Monster from my Graveyard!

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.790
Be revived! Manipulative Druid Wyd!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.630
Then I shall how you <i>my</i> Number!

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.800
I Overlay the Level Four Druid Drewes and Wyd!

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.600
With these two Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.390
Xyz Summon!

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.230
Appear, Number 44!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:48.410
Oh eternal laborer, now is the time to arise from your ancient sleep!

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.870
Become the wings that soar through the sky!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.750
Sky Pegasus the White Winged Horse!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.790
The Number has appeared!

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.840
This Number will impose a new trial onto you.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.510
I activate Sky Pegasus' effect!

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:09.010
I detach one Overlay Unit to destroy one opposing Monster!

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.640
I shall destroy Aspiring Emperor - Hope.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.850
What?!

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:19.190
However, if you pay 500 of your Life, you can negate the effect.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.110
My Life again...!

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:26.070
Yuma, if you lose Hope, you can't save Shark and the other guy.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.150
I know.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:33.330
I pay 500 points of my Life to negate Hope's destruction.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:37.620
At this moment, the other effect of Sky Pegasus activates!

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.170
When the opponent pays life points, the same amount is inflicted as damage to him!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.550
Yuma! Astral!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.180
If that goes on, our Life will be rapidly scraped away!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.100
That Number is part of his combo, too.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.060
One thing after another... What the hell is going on?!

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.150
Yuma...

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.950
Ryouga, Yuma started a Duel over here.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.160
What?

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.160
All of a sudden, a Number Spirit appeared...

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:16.870
Number Spirit?

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.040
This guy is...?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:23.170
Shark, the traps that have been set for you guys are linked to this Duel!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:27.130
When we attacked, the door on your side opened.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:28.590
What!?

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:33.010
But if we attack, his combo to diminish our Life activates.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.390
Damn! So he locked us down completely.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:41.310
Hold on, Shark! I'll definitely save you!

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.440
With friends...

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:48.030
Their inner value will be called to question, once they are separated from each other.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.070
Separated from each other...

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:53.820
Shark!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:58.490
Is there anything that seems like a hint for the Duel in your place over there?

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.500
A hint for the Duel?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.460
So, is there anything?

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.380
No...

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.170
Are those... wall paintings?

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:11.970
That's it!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:17.850
The trial he has set up for us
is some sort of mystery game!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:23.020
If separating us like that was the start of the trial,

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.060
then the location of yours, Shark, should hold some hint to solve the mystery!

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.690
Ryouga, what's drawn on the wall painting?

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:34.410
What...? There's some pictures and some sort of scripture...

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.410
This...

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:38.410
...tells of the legend about an ancient Hero.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.200
You... can read that?

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.210
The legend goes like this.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:48.210
Long long ago, there was a group of brave knights who served a certain land.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.710
One of them was a Hero that rode his beloved steed, the Pegasus.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:56.840
The knights, led by the Hero, protected the peace of that country.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.100
One day, the Hero left the castle,

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:02.980
to go back to his hometown.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.310
However, when the Hero was gone,

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.520
the knights that were left behind overthrew the king,

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.030
and took over the country.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.150
With their Hero gone, they grew conceited with their own power,

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.030
and began to deem themselves worthy to be called Kings.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.120
Who on earth are you...?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.880
Just what does this old legend mean for us...?

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.920
The rest of the Legend isn't here...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.640
Ryouga! You have to finish the Duel right away!

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.100
Understood!

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.480
My turn! Draw!

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.860
Yuma! Attack!

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.650
Even if we cut down our Life, to save Shark and Nasch,

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.240
we've got to destroy the enemy's Numbers!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:03.410
Sure! Aspiring Emperor - Hope, attack Sky Pegasus!

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:06.500
Continuous Trap, Shield of Conspiracy, activate!

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.080
This card can be used as an Equip Card for my Monster.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:14.670
Once per turn, when the equipped Monster is attacked, the battle damage will be zero,

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:16.380
and its destruction is negated!

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:22.390
At this moment...

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:27.520
...the Continuous Magic, Labyrinth of Decisions, and the Continuous Trap, Unfair Treaty, activate their effects!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.520
With this, you pay 600 Life,

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.730
and then you send one card from your hand to the Graveyard.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.110
Damn!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.160
Then the effect of Sky Pegasus activates.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:52.130
When the opponent pays Life Points, the same amount is inflicted as damage to him!

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:57.420
Yuma!

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:06.470
I will... set one card and end my turn!

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:09.890
Shark, do the wall paintings go on in that room?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.900
Yeah, they do!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.400
This is what follows.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.780
Hearing about the knights' rebellion, the Hero rushed back to the castle.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:21.070
Then the Hero appealed to them.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:25.120
Saying all that time, they had their hearts filled with justice,

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:29.040
and tried to make them remember their bonds as comrades that fought together.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.040
But his former comrades...

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.170
turned their swords against the Hero.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.760
The Hero could not kill his comrades.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:43.890
He kept refusing to fight back and thus was struck down by the swords of his own comrades.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.640
Then suddenly...

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:51.440
...his beloved steed Pegasus stood in front of the knights, trying to protect his master.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.230
With its life forfeit, it was trying to protect the Hero.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.330
And then... And what happened then?!

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:09.250
Sorry, but that's all.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.460
It's too worn after that, so I can't read any further.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.710
Tha-That's...

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.130
<i>What's with that feeling...?</i>

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.130
<i>It's like I should know this legend.</i>

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.720
<i>Don't tell me... Why...?</i>

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.720
<i>Did I come here before?</i>

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:31.180
My turn! Draw!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:35.150
I detach one Overlay Unit from Sky Pegasus,

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.150
to destroy the opponent's Monster!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:43.990
However, by paying 500 Life, you can negate this effect.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.280
Come. It is time for your trial!

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.950
Yuma! If you deplete your Life any further, you can't win this Duel!

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.290
Don't worry about us! Let Hope be destroyed!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.170
Well, what will you do?

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:00.460
Will you pay 500 to protect Hope or...?

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:08.010
To protect your friends, you need to protect Hope, Yuma!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:09.930
Wha-what do you mean?!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.180
You don't need to butt in!

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:17.400
I know the rest of the legend!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:25.820
It was impossible for the Hero to abandon the Pegasus.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.790
He stayed together with the Pegasus as he passed away.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.710
Don't you understand?!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:45.220
This legend is telling us about one's attitude to believe in and protect their friends!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.720
Yuma, protect Hope! Believe me!

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:51.310
Why do you know all that?!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.020
As I thought, you're...!

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:01.190
Ryouga!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.200
That's right, Ryouga! I am...

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:09.870
I am...

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.080
I am a Barian!

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.170
You're... Durbe!

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.590
Yuma, don't believe what this guy is saying! He's a Barian!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.720
No way! That guy is a Barian?!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.430
Yuma! Are you trying to make the same mistake all over again?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.310
<i>"Good work saving me back there."</i>

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.190
<i>"Officer Yuma"!</i>

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:45.730
Yuma...

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.990
I... I...

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:56.120
Yuma, whatever you believe in, trust in yourself.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:01.130
Come! Try to overcome this trial!

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:04.290
Sky Pegasus, destroy Hope!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:10.470
I will pay with my Life to negate Hope's destruction!

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:13.800
What?!

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.850
At this moment, Sky Pegasus' effect activates!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.810
When the opponent pays Life Points, he receives the same amount as damage!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.450
With this, we have just 200 Life left.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:36.620
I- I see! So that's how it was...!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.960
Yuma! Why are you doing what he tells you?!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:47.210
Shark, there <i>is</i> no doubt in me.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.380
I don't want to doubt... anyone!

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.380
Yuma...

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.470
Here goes!

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.720
My turn! Draw!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:00.680
Yuma! Now his combo is broken ! Attack him!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.190
Astral...

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:07.900
I don't get why, but if you say so, let's go!

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.280
Hope, attack Sky Pegasus!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.700
Trap, activate! Shield of Conspiracy!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:24.120
With the effect of Labyrinth of Decisions, you send one card from your hand to the Graveyard...

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:32.840
Damn! I send one card to the Graveyard!

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:36.260
With this, Yuma will get 600 damage and lose.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.890
It's alright. Yuma definitely won't.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:42.810
Huh?

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.390
Nothing happened?

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:47.690
What... on earth...

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.530
His combo no longer can activate.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:54.530
Originally, because of his combo with Labyrinth of Decisions,

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.910
he himself has to pay the costs.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:01.330
And due to Unfair Treaty, we had to pay.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:05.750
But by protecting Hope from Sky Pegasus' effect,

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.040
We only have 200 Life Points left.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.420
The condition to keep up his combo was broken

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:14.220
when we had less than 600 Life Points.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.930
Now that we no longer have enough Life to pay,

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.720
he has to pay for it with his own Life.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.650
Your choice was right!

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.020
Go, Yuma!

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:31.820
Right!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.150
Now that we know that, I'll use what I sent to the Graveyard before!

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:37.860
Counter Trap, Hyper Quick, activate!

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.950
When this card is sent from the hand to the Graveyard,

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:45.250
I can draw one card from my deck, and if it's a Magic Card,

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.330
it is treated as a Quick Play Magic!

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.500
Yuma, this is a Destiny Draw!

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.210
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:54.760
Draw!

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.680
It's here!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:01.930
I activate the Rank-Up Magic, Numeron Force!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:06.020
This card can Rank-Up one Xyz Monster!

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.900
I Overlay the Rank Four Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:15.150
With this Monster, I rebuild the Overlay Network!

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.200
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.780
Show yourself, Chaos Number 39!

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:26.080
Let your shining soul of hope embrace the universe!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.580
Be the power to lead us to the future!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:34.210
Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray Victory!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.560
I activate Hope Ray Victory's effect!

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:49.350
When this Monster battles, I can detach one Overlay Unit

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:53.730
then the Attack Power of the opposing Monster is added to his!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.320
Victory Charge!

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:04.160
Go! Hope Ray - Victory!

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:08.330
Hope Sword Double Victory Slash!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:27.560
We... we won..

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.940
You have overcome the trial.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:44.030
Mach, tell me, the Pegasus who served the Hero... was it you?

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.870
Yes. There still is another part of the legend.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.500
The knights' hearts were struck by the willingness of the Hero and Pegasus to sacrifice their lives.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.040
They were ashamed of themselves, and their desire for rebellion vanished.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.340
They buried the Pegasus and the Hero with honor,

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:06.100
kneeling before their grave, their heads hanging low.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:12.810
And then, the Hero, together with Pegasus' soul, was called to Heaven.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:16.520
This is the whole legend.

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:18.900
Yuma, Astral...

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.780
You both should try betting on your strength...

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:23.160
...to trust in others.

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.130
Number 44...

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.340
Why did you help us?

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.670
I don't know.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:46.300
In a manner of speaking, perhaps it was because my heart was moved by the legend of this ruin.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.140
Durbe!

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.310
Thank you, man!

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.140
If you hadn't told me about how the legend goes on...

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.940
No, it was your choice.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:59.900
Because you would have trusted it even without listening to it.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.860
But this nonsense ends here and now.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:07.950
The next time we meet, we'll settle things once and for all.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:14.290
Durbe...

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.760
This is...!

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.760
A Conqueror's Coin!

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.840
What's that?

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.140
My dad...

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:33.100
To prove he went somewhere really dangerous, he had a habit of leaving coins like these behind.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.850
Then your father was here after all...

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.230
Yes... My dad...

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.900
I'm sure he's been watching my Duels from somewhere far away.

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.990
Astral, Shark... I've done a lot of thinking...

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:52.160
Those Barian guys may take advantage of the fact that I trust in people...

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:56.830
But I just can't bring myself to doubt people.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.170
All I can do is trust in them.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:03.260
<i>If that is your conclusion, I won't say anything for now.</i>

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:09.220
<i>Even if it means you end up taking a different path from me in the future.</i>

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:24.070
<i>Is it the world that's boring?</i>

00:22:24.070 --> 00:22:26.610
<i>Or maybe you're the one who's not gettin' serious?</i>

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:27.820
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:29.240
<i>Do I understand?</i>

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:32.120
<i>Already got my answers</i>

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:34.620
<i>Once you start movin', you ain't stoppin'</i>

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:37.160
<i>I go on thinkin' even while losin'.</i>

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:38.250
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:39.290
<i>I understand!</i>

00:22:39.290 --> 00:22:42.670
<i>Our formula for reversal's already gathered</i>

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:45.010
<i>You afraid it ain't comin' true?</i>

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:48.130
<i>I gotta 'least give it a try</i>

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.340
<i>Ain't no problem if they say I'm borin'</i>

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:53.350
<i>True failure's when we stop movin'</i>

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:55.310
<i>Come on! Ga, ga, ga, guys & dolls</i>

00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:56.680
<i>Go, go, go, go my way</i>

00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:58.560
<i>Oh, oh, oh, over ray</i>

00:22:58.850 --> 00:23:02.860
<i>Door's always open for you</i>

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:07.940
<i>Bring your power forth and go way, go way</i>

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:09.200
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:13.200
<i>And tears are no way, no way</i>

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:18.580
<i>With all my strength, pave way, go way</i>

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:19.790
<i>I understand!</i>

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:23.920
<i>Got all the courage here</i>

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:26.090
<i>You ought to understand!</i>

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:28.300
<i>Go way, go way</i>

00:23:41.310 --> 00:23:44.360
The next location is some ruins across the distant seas.

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:48.280
But Number 96 and Vector suddenly appeared there!

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:51.150
I won't allow them to take the Number!

00:23:51.150 --> 00:23:53.070
They plan to get in our way...!

00:23:53.070 --> 00:23:54.530
The royal palace...!

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:56.370
Run away! These ruins are a trap!

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.700
You... have the power of the Barians?!

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.370
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:05.000
"The Cunning Vector - Astral vs. Number 96"

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.710
I will be your opponent!

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:08.460
Number 96!
